1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Home is calling.

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Aquaman is a action, adventure, fantasy film directed by James Wan.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Half-human, half-Atlantean Arthur Curry is taken on the journey of his
lifetime to discover if he is worth of being a king.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Arthur Curry / Aquaman, played by Jason Momoa.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Mera, played by Amber Heard.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Nuidis Vulko, played by Willem Dafoe.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
King Orm Marius / Ocean Master, played by Patrick Wilson.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Atlanna, played by Nicole Kidman.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
King Nereus, played by Dolph Lundgren.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Aquaman is a 2018 American superhero film based on
the DC character of the same name.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Co-produced and distributed by Warner Bros.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Pictures, it is the sixth film in the DC Extended Universe (DCEU).

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Directed by James Wan from a screenplay by David Leslie Johnson-McGoldrick and Will Beall, it stars Jason Momoa as Arthur Curry / Aquaman, who sets out to lead the
underwater kingdom of Atlantis and stop his evil half-brother, King Orm (Patrick Wilson) from uniting the seven underwater kingdoms to destroy the surface world.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
Amber Heard, Willem Dafoe, Dolph Lundgren, Yahya Abdul-Mateen II,
and Nicole Kidman also star in supporting roles.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
Development began in 2004 but did not gain traction
until Man of Steel was released in 2013.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
In August 2014, Beall and Kurt Johnstad were hired to write competing scripts.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
Wan signed on as director in April 2015, and in July 2016, the
film moved forward with Beall's screenplay.

18
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
The main cast was confirmed through 2016 and early 2017.

19
01:44:30,000 --> 01:44:36,000
Principal photography began in Australia in May 2017, taking place at Village Roadshow Studios on the Gold
Coast, Queensland, Australia, with additional production teams in Canada, Italy, and Morocco.

20
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
Filming concluded the following October.

21
01:55:30,000 --> 01:55:36,000
Several vendors provided visual effects and animation, ranging from high-detail
hair simulations to the creation of CGI animals and locations.

22
02:01:00,000 --> 02:01:06,000
Aquaman premiered in London on November 26, 2018, and was
released in the United States on December 21.

23
02:06:30,000 --> 02:06:36,000
While the film received mixed reviews from critics, it grossed $1.152 billion worldwide, making it the highest-grossing DCEU film, the highest-grossing film based
on a DC Comics character, the fifth-highest-grossing film of 2018, and (at the time of its release) the 20th highest-grossing film of all time.

24
02:12:00,000 --> 02:12:06,000
A sequel, Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom, was released on December 22, 2023, while a non-canonical animated
miniseries, Aquaman: King of Atlantis, is set after the events of this film and was released in October 2021.

25
02:17:30,000 --> 02:17:36,000
The film explores themes of hero, chase, atlantis, superhero, half-brother.
